propertyDetails.actionTwo=ask us to remove the property from the Council Tax list if it has been demolished, is derelict, or is undergoing major renovation
propertyDetails.signIn=You'll need a GOV Gateway or GOV.UK One Login Account to sign in.
propertyDetails.print=Print this page
propertyDetails.searchAnother=Search for another property

selfCert.title=Are you responsible for the Council Tax on this property?
selfCert.heading=Are you responsible for the Council Tax on this property?
selfCert.guidance=Only people who are responsible for the Council Tax on this property have permission to view more details. This includes people acting for someone who is responsible.
selfCert.warning=If you are not responsible for the Council Tax on this property, you should not continue with this service.
selfCert.actingForSomeone=I am acting for someone who is responsible
selfCert.permissionHint=You will need their written permission
selfCert.error.required=Select whether you are responsible for the Council Tax on this property

uploadEvidence.title = Upload Evidence
uploadEvidence.p1 = The file must be a PDF or image (PNG or JPG) and be less than 25MB.

bandReview.title = Request a Council Tax band review
bandReview.heading = Request a Council Tax band review

bandReview.introduction = You can ask the VO (Valuation Office) for a Council Tax band review at any time.

bandReview.noCharge = There is no charge for this service.

bandReview.evidenceIntroduction = You will need to tell us why you think the band should be reviewed. We may ask you for more details, and you may be required to provide evidence to support your request.

bandReview.when.heading = When you can request a Council Tax band review

bandReview.when.introduction = You can request a review of your Council Tax band if:

bandReview.when.bullet.1 = you became the new taxpayer within the last 6 months
bandReview.when.bullet.2 = the Council Tax band has changed in the last 6 months
bandReview.when.bullet.3 = the local area has physically changed

bandReview.changes.introduction = You can also request a review if something has changed. For example, the property:

bandReview.changes.bullet.1 = has been demolished
bandReview.changes.bullet.2 = is derelict and cannot be lived in
bandReview.changes.bullet.3 = is undergoing major renovations or repairs
bandReview.changes.bullet.4 = is partly used for business
bandReview.changes.bullet.5 = has been split into multiple properties or merged into one
bandReview.appeal = If you request a review for one of these reasons, but do not agree with the outcome, you can appeal the decision.
bandReview.improvements = We will take any improvements into account when setting the new band, which could be higher than the previous one. The new band will usually take effect from the date the property becomes fit to live in again.
bandReview.localCouncil.heading = Contacting your Local Council
bandReview.localCouncil.guidance = You should also check with your local council for advice and information about Council Tax. Visit your local council's website for more details.
bandReview.otherReason.heading = Reviewing the band for any other reason
bandReview.otherReason.evidence = If none of the above apply, we will only review your band if you provide supporting evidence. Your request for a band review will be rejected without this.
bandReview.otherReason.appeal = You will not have any legal rights to appeal the outcome of a review.

scenario.title = Choose which applies to you
scenario.heading = Choose which applies to you
scenario.lessThanSixMonths = I’ve been responsible for paying Council Tax for less than 6 months
scenario.moreThanSixMonths = I’ve been responsible for paying Council Tax for more than 6 months
scenario.bandChanged = My Council Tax band was changed by the Valuation Office (VO) in the last 6 months
scenario.propertyOrAreaChanged = There have been changes made to my home or in the local area
scenario.other = Other
scenario.error.required = Select which applies to you

formalReview.title = Asking for a formal review
formalReview.heading = Asking for a formal review
formalReview.selection.before = You have told us that you’ve been responsible for paying Council Tax on your home for
formalReview.selection.answer = less than 6 months.
formalReview.introduction = This means that you can ask for a formal review of your Council Tax band. This is also known as a ‘Formal Challenge’ or ‘Making a Proposal’.
formalReview.changeSelection = You can change your selection if this option is not right for you.
formalReview.howItWorks.heading = How a formal review works
formalReview.table.caption = Information about how a formal review works
formalReview.whatItIs.heading = What it is
formalReview.whatItIs.content = You can ask the Valuation Office (VO) to review the Council Tax band your home is in.
formalReview.whatItIsFor.heading = What it’s for
formalReview.whatItIsFor.content = You can ask for a formal review if you think that your home is in the wrong Council Tax band.
formalReview.when.heading = When you can ask for a formal review
formalReview.when.before = If you have been responsible for the Council Tax on your home for
formalReview.when.answer = less than 6 months.
formalReview.duration.heading = How long it takes
formalReview.duration.content = Up to 16 weeks
formalReview.evidenceRequired.heading = Evidence required
formalReview.evidenceRequired.content = You do not need to provide any evidence. However, any information you give us will help the VO understand why you think your home should be in a different band.
formalReview.evidenceExamples.heading = Examples of evidence
formalReview.evidenceExamples.bullet.1 = addresses of similar homes in a lower band than yours
formalReview.evidenceExamples.bullet.2 = the price that your home or similar homes sold for between 1 April 2001 and 31 March 2005
formalReview.evidenceExamples.bullet.3 = you can submit written evidence and upload up to 5 files including PDFs, documents and photos
formalReview.decision.heading = Decision
formalReview.decision.introduction = There are 3 possible decisions that can be made:
formalReview.decision.bullet.1 = your home stays in the same band
formalReview.decision.bullet.2 = your home is moved into a lower band
formalReview.decision.bullet.3 = your home is moved into a higher band
formalReview.afterDecision.heading = After a decision has been made
formalReview.afterDecision.content = You have 4 months after the date of the decision to appeal to the Valuation Tribunal Wales if you are not satisfied with the outcome.

responsibleFromDate.error.required = Enter the date you became responsible for paying Council Tax
responsibleFromDate.error.twoRequired = The date you became responsible for paying Council Tax must include a day, month and year
